%erg 0.1
Title: make regen-assets should run erg check to gate ticket/asset edits locally
Created: 2026-06-18
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-06-18T09:33Z HDMX-coding-agent created

--- body ---

## Context

The asset/ticket-close edit path has no local gate. `make regen-assets` only
copies `src/go/assets/{.ergrc,AGENTS.md}` into `tickets/` (Makefile ~line 92) --
it runs no validation. So store-shape violations reach CI before anyone notices.

PR #305 (ticket 0244) shipped a closed ticket left in `tickets/` instead of
`tickets/closed/`; `erg check` would have caught it instantly, but nothing ran
`erg check` locally, so it failed only in the `test-check` CI job. A local gate
turns that into an immediate, cheap signal.

Sibling ticket 0245 covers the ASCII-asset half of the same gap (extending the
test-init guard to .ergrc). This ticket covers the store-integrity half.

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` (~line 92, `regen-assets:` target) -- currently a bare two-line copy
- `src/go/check.go` -- the `erg check` implementation invoked by the gate

## Actions
1. Make `regen-assets` depend on `build` and run `./build/erg check` after the
   copy (or add a small `check-store` target wired into the pre-commit hook), so
   an unarchived closed ticket / duplicate ID / folder-closure violation fails
   locally before push. Pick whichever fits the existing hook layout -- a
   pre-commit hook is stronger than coupling it to regen-assets, since most
   ticket edits don't touch assets.

## Test
- Red step: a closed-but-unarchived ticket in `tickets/` must make the new gate
  (or the pre-commit hook) exit non-zero. Cover via a test in `tests/` that
  invokes the gate against a fixture store with a planted violation.

## Invariants
- Existing `make build` / `make test` targets keep working unchanged.
- The gate must not require network access.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A store violation (closed-but-unarchived, duplicate ID) fails a local
      command before push -- not only in CI
- [ ] A test exercises the gate against a planted violation
- [ ] `make test` green on the clean tree
